2026-09-27 00:03 Done as decided 2026-09-27 (coordinator). Cilium.pm: _require_running replaced by _require_deployed_release($release), which upgrade_cilium calls right after _read_release, before _read_running. It checks pending-upgrade/pending-rollback first and dies through a new shared helper _die_release_stuck, which _release_action now uses as well (install_cilium and upgrade_cilium give byte-identical messages; the test compares them). Then, without a deployed revision (no release, failed first install, pending-install, uninstalling, uninstalled, even with cilium-config/DaemonSet present), it dies pointing to install_cilium; when a release exists, the message says install_cilium removes what is left and installs again. A failed upgrade over a deployed revision still upgrades. pending-install OVER a deployed revision (a state Helm should not produce) goes to stuck, following the maintainer's rule that pending-* means a Helm operation hangs. $running->{present} removed: nobody used it anymore. POD of upgrade_cilium updated. t/cilium.t: k66 subtest rewritten (a: 8 cases, b: 4 cases, same message install vs upgrade, 403 on the DaemonSet without a release -> missing release wins, 403 with deployed release -> dies as itself, k3s without host, 3 upgrade cases), every die case checks no host commands, no CRDs, no values file. The k3s-host upgrade test got a deployed release. Red against HEAD's Cilium.pm; prove -lr t/ green: 31 files, 653 tests, 0 'uninitialized'. Unverified live: upgrade_cilium against a real cluster (kubernetes-ocp). Also found (not touched, for the coordinator): install_cilium's _release_action returns 'reinstall' for pending-install even when has_deployed, and _purge_release then deletes every revision Secret incl. the deployed one after 'cilium uninstall'. Unreachable with normal Helm (pending-install exists only on a first install), but if it ever occurs it takes down the pod network; upgrade_cilium now dies stuck there instead.

